<file path="projects.directives/social-pub/social-publisher-post-asset-kit.md">
# Social Publisher -- Portfolio Post Asset Kit

## Purpose
This kit aggregates the assets and guidance needed for a portfolio post or VC-grade announcement about Social Publisher (by Flat 18). It includes ready-made visual assets, a screen capture list, feature highlights, and copy blocks.

## Where the assets live
Existing assets are already generated in these folders:
- `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/`
- `gen-assets/social-publisher-graphics-assets/`

Use these as placeholders now and replace with live product screenshots once the app is running.

## Primary visuals (ready to use)
Brand and share imagery:
- Wordmarks and lockups: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/brand/`
- App icon: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/brand/app-icon-512.png`
- Open Graph share image: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/brand/og-social-share-1200x630.png`
- X/Twitter card: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/brand/twitter-x-card-800x418.png`

Hero and feature previews:
- Hero mockup: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/landing/hero/hero-composer-mockup-dark.webp`
- Feature tiles:
  - Composer: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/landing/features/feature-composer-640x400.webp`
  - Calendar: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/landing/features/feature-calendar-640x400.webp`
  - Channel connections: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/landing/features/feature-channel-connections-640x400.webp`
  - Publishing log: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/landing/features/feature-publishing-log-640x400.webp`

Illustrations (optional for narrative sections):
- How it works steps: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/how-it-works/`
- Empty states: `gen-assets/social-publisher-assets/empty-states/`

## Screen capture list (replace placeholders when available)
Capture these screens to show real product depth. Suggested views and focus areas:
1. Composer -- show base post + per-platform variants, validation panel, and preview tabs.
2. Calendar -- week view with drag/drop cards and a reschedule modal.
3. Media library -- grid view with metadata and preview drawer.
4. Channels -- connected accounts, permission status, and reconnect hints.
5. Logs -- published + failed jobs with retry controls.
6. Settings -- AI provider keys (BYO model) and workspace settings.

Recommended capture notes:
- Use a populated workspace name and 6-10 scheduled posts across 2-3 platforms.
- Include at least one warning state (validation or media constraints).
- Capture both light and dark themes if available.
- Use 2x resolution and export WebP + PNG.

## Feature showcase (copy + visual pairing)
Use these for a carousel or sectioned post:
- Compose once, tailor everywhere -- Pair with Composer screenshot.
- Calendar scheduling that stays reliable -- Pair with Calendar screenshot.
- Media library built for reuse -- Pair with Media Library screenshot.
- Transparent logs and retries -- Pair with Publishing Log screenshot.
- BYO AI keys for cost control -- Pair with Settings screenshot.

## Solution narrative (carousel storyboard)
Slide 1 -- The problem
- Fragmented platform rules + expensive tools = slow, inconsistent publishing.

Slide 2 -- The workflow fix
- Compose once, then apply platform-aware variants and validations.

Slide 3 -- Reliability
- A dedicated worker pipeline handles scheduled publishing with retries and logs.

Slide 4 -- Cost + control
- BYO AI keys and a lean stack keep pricing predictable.

Slide 5 -- Open architecture
- Open-source connectors and capability rules keep the platform adaptable.

## Copy blocks (VC-style)
One-liner:
- A platform-aware social publisher built for speed, reliability, and affordability.

Elevator pitch (2-3 sentences):
- Social Publisher helps teams compose once, validate per platform, and schedule posts with confidence. A dedicated queue-based publishing pipeline and transparent logs reduce risk, while BYO AI keys keep costs predictable. It is built for smaller teams and agencies who need reliability without enterprise overhead.

Feature bullets:
- Multi-platform composer with per-platform variants
- Live validation against platform capabilities
- Drag-and-drop scheduling calendar
- Media library with reusable assets
- Publishing logs with retry controls
- Optional BYO AI copy generation

Open-source rationale (short):
- Open connectors and validation rules keep the system transparent, extensible, and resilient to platform API changes.

CTA options:
- Join the beta
- Follow the build
- Request access

## Format guidance (industry standard)
- Export masters in 1:1 and 16:9; optionally 4:5 for mobile-heavy feeds.
- Keep text safe margins (10-12% padding) for platform cropping.
- Provide WebP for web use and PNG for fallback.
- Target file size under ~2-3 MB per image to avoid compression artifacts.

## Checklist
- Replace placeholder screenshots with real product captures.
- Verify brand usage: correct wordmark and lockup.
- Validate that any metrics shown match current data.
- Ensure images have descriptive alt text for accessibility.
- Keep the post narrative aligned with the open-source plan and roadmap.
